My own preference here is to two weapon, with GDSM, a robe and
the amulet of reflection.  IMHO, it's worth being able to use
some spells---you can get cure sickness to 0% failure, for
example, and that's very, very useful when you meet some
monsters.  (Otherwise, practically, you've got to save some
potions of extra healing, which weigh a lot.)  Magic missle
ain't too bad either, and cone of cold is your special spell.
Fixed up like that:
 -- If you can afford to let them get near you, you can just
    wack away.  One turn is enough for most monsters.
 -- If you don't even want to let them close, fire away with
    daggers.
 -- And for places where you don't want to use daggers (like
    where there's a lot of water around), you've got your attack
    spells.
And of course, don't forget to be fast (e.g. speed boots).
Those extra moves can be a lifesaver.  (Dual weaponing
Grayswandir and a silver saber, and playing the speed system
right, so I got two hits before he got his first one, I was able
to kill Orcus without him touching me, or even having time to
teleport away.  More generally, speed allows you to manoeuver
around the big baddies, to fight them where you want to.  In
other words, where you have their only escape path blocked.)

